messages:
maria: heads-up, opened a PR to expand the Troubleshooting -> Error reference with a small 'context limits' workflow and a practical fallback example when you hit token ceilings. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1456 :memo:
kevin: looks useful. pls include JS + Python SDK snippets and a tiny retry template customers can paste. :thumbsup:
maria: added both. here's the compact JS pattern I included for 429 + backoff:
```js
for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
  try {
    const res = await client.generate({ prompt });
    break;
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 'TooManyRequests') {
      await sleep(100 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
      continue;
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
// fallback: try truncating messages or switch to embeddings-based retrieval
```
sam: can we show a micro-algo for trimming context (drop whole messages until under token budget; prefer oldest assistant/user turns first)? helps product folks.
maria: added pseudocode and a one-line rule: "remove entire messages rather than slicing tokens; prefer dropping system and earliest user turns."
olga: found two stale cross-links in the error-ref (CLI troubleshooting, SDK retry-policy). I'll prepare a tiny link-fix PR after this lands. pinging @docs-ci to run link checks.
docs-ci: running link-checker on branch docs/ctx-fallbacks (build #5979).
kevin: also add a caution about partial outputs when truncating — recommend validating function-calls or schema after the model returns. saves downstream bugs.
maria: added a 2-sentence caveat plus a schema-guard snippet. also mentioned an alternative fallback: use embeddings+retrieval for throughput-sensitive paths.
olga: SGTM. I'll run linter locally and then merge once docs-ci is green. thanks :sparkles:
docs-ci: link-checker finished: 2 warnings, 0 failures. warnings: very long external URLs (consider shortlinking).
maria: merged and added a short changelog blurb for the next docs release.
